the coolest since 2019.","t_yest":"November 13: cooler than 80% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>39\u00b0F</strong> was the 24th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 125 since 1902, the coolest since 2019. The normal high for the date is 49\u00b0F, and the record is 71\u00b0F (1902). The low of <strong>32\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Syracuse has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Syracuse's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Syracuse has set <strong class=\"sig\">32 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 79 that chance alone would give, and <strong>117 record highs</strong>, more than the 79 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (51). Syracuse's all-time high is 102\u00b0F, on July 9, 1936.","t_chg":"Syracuse's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 123 complete years: Syracuse's average low shows no clear change: +0.07\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.15) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. Syracuse's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.33\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.24 to +0.41), about +4.0\u00b0F since 1903. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.82\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.40 to +1.25) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.64\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.20 to +1.08). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Syracuse has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Syracuse's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.61 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.32 to +0.90), about +7.5 inches since 1903. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 39.7 inches a year. The wettest year was 1976 (58.17 in); the driest, 1908 (26.96 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 5 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}